 "date": "2026-11-19",
 "title": "The run already contains the intervention, and the intervention is not the bottleneck",
 "the_answer": "Retention is solved and identification is not. The counterfactual that identification needs can be manufactured for free from a single failing run -- flipping one firing of one guard costs one bit and about half a second -- and executing it on a fresh blind corpus of 15 real commits reaches the human's changed line 3 times, the human's expression 0 times. Five single-firing flips turned the failing test green; all five broke other tests in the same file and none admitted an exact-fit refinement, so a version of this round without those two gates would have claimed five repairs it cannot defend. The single bottleneck is therefore not the observation, not the parameters (zero) and not the index: it is the replacement expression -- the content of the fix, which the failing run never produces.",
