 "erratum_on_the_previous_round": "The previous round's 29-commit population was hand-built from four libraries and partly studied while the tool was built; click@1b0e19f505 is the commit the blame chain was derived on and is reported here as IN_SAMPLE, not as generalization. This round changes the population first and measures both arms on it, and the difference is the whole result: 1 verified repair in-sample, 0 out of 15 fresh commits for either arm.",
 "the_single_bottleneck": "The replacement expression. The run names the place and the discrepancy (the flip reached the human's changed line 3 of 15 times at one bit per candidate), and it does not name the value that should have been there: 12 of the 15 fixes are a value the failing run never produced (an attribute name, a regex, an argument, a call's routing) and 3 are behaviour that did not exist, which INSUFFICIENCY_CERTIFICATE_20261113_V1 proves no trace can supply.",
 "falsifier": "This round's claim dies if a mechanism that forces the VALUE at a flip-identified firing and synthesizes the replacement expression from the artifact's own vocabulary does not beat 0/15 on a fresh corpus of this construction, or beats it only by reading the commit's diff. The user's claim dies if any of the fifteen is repaired by supplying the right action once and repeating it.",
